        content: "DSCR is one of several ratios lenders watch, and it answers a different question from each of the others:\n\n- **Loan-to-value (LTV)** asks how much of the property's value is borrowed. It is about the collateral; DSCR is about the cash flow.\n- **Debt yield** (NOI divided by the loan amount) is another cash-flow test, and some lenders prefer it because it does not depend on the interest rate or amortization schedule.\n- **Cash-on-cash return** measures the return on your equity \u2014 the cash left after debt service, divided by the cash you invested. DSCR tells you whether the loan is safe; cash-on-cash tells you whether the deal is worth it to you.\n\nA good deal usually passes all of them. A deal that passes DSCR but fails debt yield, or passes LTV but fails DSCR, is a deal to look at more closely before committing.",
