        content: "DSCR = NOI \u00f7 annual debt service. It is the test most likely to kill a deal, because the lender applies it, not you. Typical floors vary by lender and property type \u2014 these are the common reference points, not a universal rule: agency multifamily loans (Fannie Mae, Freddie Mac) typically require a 1.25x minimum; most commercial lenders look for 1.20x\u20131.25x on stabilized multifamily; office and retail typically face 1.25x\u20131.35x; hospitality typically 1.35x and up.\n\n- [ ] **Computed with the real loan terms.** **Pass:** the rate and amortization come from a written quote or term sheet. **Fail:** a teaser rate, or an interest-only assumption that will not survive closing.\n- [ ] **At or above the lender's floor.** **Pass:** DSCR meets the floor for your loan type (1.25x for agency multifamily). **Fail:** below the floor \u2014 the lender will shrink the loan and you will have to add equity.\n- [ ] **Tested on trailing-12 NOI.** **Pass:** DSCR is computed on actuals, not pro forma. **Fail:** DSCR only works on projected income.\n\nUse the [DSCR calculator](https://crecalculators.com/en/calculators/dscr/) to run the check.",
