        content: "The deal: a 20-unit apartment building, $750 per unit per month, asking price $1,600,000. The buyer sets the hurdles first: cap rate at least 7.00%, DSCR at least 1.25x, cash-on-cash at least 5.00% pre-tax, break-even ratio at most 85%.\n\n**Gate 1 \u2014 income.** Gross potential rent is 20 \u00d7 $750 \u00d7 12 = $180,000. Other income (laundry and fees, verified from the trailing-12 statement) is $6,000, so potential gross income is $186,000. Vacancy and credit loss at 5% \u2014 the trailing-12 actual was 4.6%, so 5% is conservative \u2014 is 0.05 \u00d7 $186,000 = $9,300. Effective gross income is $186,000 \u2212 $9,300 = $176,700. Gate 1: **pass**.\n\n**Gate 2 \u2014 expenses.** Property taxes $18,000 (verified with the assessor); insurance $7,200 (written quote); repairs and maintenance $9,600; management at 8% of EGI = $14,136; owner-paid utilities $6,000; replacement reserves at $250 \u00d7 20 units = $5,000. Total operating expenses: $18,000 + $7,200 + $9,600 + $14,136 + $6,000 + $5,000 = $59,936. NOI is $176,700 \u2212 $59,936 = $116,764. Gate 2: **pass**.\n\n**Gate 3 \u2014 cap rate.** $116,764 \u00f7 $1,600,000 = 7.30%. The hurdle is 7.00%. Gate 3: **pass**.\n\n**Gate 4 \u2014 DSCR.** The loan is 70% loan-to-value, so $1,120,000. Terms from the lender's written quote: 6.25% interest, 25-year amortization, monthly payments. The monthly payment is $7,388.30, so annual debt service is $7,388.30 \u00d7 12 = $88,660. DSCR is $116,764 \u00f7 $88,660 = 1.32x. The hurdle is 1.25x. Gate 4: **pass**.\n\n**Gate 5 \u2014 cash-on-cash.** Initial cash is a $480,000 down payment plus $20,000 of closing costs = $500,000. Annual cash flow is $116,764 \u2212 $88,660 = $28,104. Cash-on-cash is $28,104 \u00f7 $500,000 = 5.62%. The hurdle is 5.00%. Gate 5: **pass**.\n\n**Gate 6 \u2014 break-even.** BER is ($59,936 + $88,660) \u00f7 $186,000 = $148,596 \u00f7 $186,000 = 79.9%. The hurdle is 85% or lower. Gate 6: **pass**. Stress tests: at 10% vacancy, EGI falls to $167,400, NOI to $108,208, and DSCR to 1.22x \u2014 below the 1.25x hurdle, but cash flow stays positive at $19,548. At a 7.25% rate, annual debt service rises to $97,145 and DSCR falls to 1.20x. The deal survives a bad year, but the margin against a rate rise is thin \u2014 a rate lock or a price cut is worth negotiating.\n\n**Gate 7 \u2014 Deal Analyzer.** Run the same inputs through the [Deal Analyzer](https://crecalculators.com/en/tools/deal-analyzer/). The five outputs should read: cap rate 7.30%, cash-on-cash 5.62%, DSCR 1.32x, break-even ratio 79.9%, NOI $116,764. Verdict: **all seven gates pass**. The deal is financeable at the quoted terms, with a noted watch item on rate margin.",
