    dataSources: ["Reonomy, \"Commercial Real Estate Loan Terms & Types (2026)\" \u2014 conventional commercial mortgages typically run 5- to 10-year terms amortized over 20 to 25 years. https://www.reonomy.com/resources/commercial-real-estate-loans/ (accessed November 10, 2026)", "Crestmont Capital, \"What Is a Balloon Mortgage in Commercial Lending?\" \u2014 balloon structures such as 5/25 and 7/23, and amortization schedules of 20 to 30 years. https://www.crestmontcapital.com/blog/what-is-a-balloon-mortgage-in-commercial-lending (accessed November 10, 2026)", "LegalClarity, \"How Long Are Commercial Real Estate Loans? Maturity Terms\" \u2014 CMBS loans typically carry 5- to 10-year terms with 25- to 30-year amortization. https://legalclarity.org/how-long-are-commercial-real-estate-loans-maturity-terms/ (accessed November 10, 2026)", "CommercialCafe, \"What is Amortization in Commercial Real Estate?\" \u2014 amortization versus term, and the trade-off between a lower payment and a larger balloon. https://www.commercialcafe.com/blog/amortization-commercial-real-estate/ (accessed November 10, 2026)", "Qualified Commercial, \"Refinancing a Maturing Commercial Mortgage\" \u2014 starting 12 to 18 months before maturity, and a maturing loan as a brand-new underwrite. https://www.qualifiedcommercial.com/academy/refinancing-a-maturing-commercial-mortgage (accessed November 10, 2026)", "Bancorp One, \"Commercial Real Estate Refinancing Guide & Timing\" \u2014 beginning refinance planning 6 to 9 months before maturity, and an open prepayment window in the final 30 to 90 days. https://www.bancorpone.com/guides/commercial-refinance (accessed November 10, 2026)", "All worked-example figures were calculated from the formulas shown in the article; the 6.75% rate is illustrative, not a market quote."],
