        content: "- **Set your hurdles before you see the numbers.** Write down your minimum cap rate, minimum DSCR, minimum cash-on-cash return, and maximum break-even ratio first. If you set them after seeing the deal, you will set them to make the deal pass.\n- **Use trailing-12-month actuals, not the seller's pro forma.** A pro forma is a claim about the future; actuals are evidence about the past. Where actuals do not exist, say so and treat the number as unverified.\n- **Verify each gate with your own calculation.** Run the numbers in the site's calculators, then confirm the full chain in the [Deal Analyzer](https://crecalculators.com/en/tools/deal-analyzer/). If your hand check and the tool disagree, find the input that differs \u2014 do not trust either one blindly.\n- **Record pass or fail at each gate.** One fail means stop. Renegotiate, restructure, or walk.",
