        content: "Expenses are where most deals are undersold. A missing expense is worth exactly as much as a fake dollar of income.\n\n- [ ] **Taxes verified with the assessor.** **Pass:** the tax figure matches the assessor's current assessed value times the tax rate, or it includes the reassessment a sale will trigger. **Fail:** the seller uses last year's bill when a reassessment is due.\n- [ ] **Insurance quoted, not copied.** **Pass:** a written quote in hand. **Fail:** the seller's old premium copied forward.\n- [ ] **Management budgeted even if you self-manage.** Management typically runs 6\u201310% of effective gross income. **Pass:** a management line exists in the budget. **Fail:** no management cost because \"I'll manage it myself\" \u2014 your time is not free, and a lender will underwrite the cost anyway.\n- [ ] **Replacement reserves budgeted.** A commonly cited underwriting allowance for multifamily is $250\u2013$300 per unit per year. **Pass:** reserves are deducted before NOI. **Fail:** NOI is computed with no reserves.\n- [ ] **Expenses cross-checked against actuals.** **Pass:** underwritten expenses are within 10% of trailing-12 actuals, or every difference is explained. **Fail:** pro forma expenses are more than 10% below actuals with no reason given.\n- [ ] **No missing category.** Utilities, repairs, administration, legal, turnover costs \u2014 every category has a number, or an explicit zero with a reason.\n\nThe formula: NOI = EGI \u2212 operating expenses. Debt service, income taxes, depreciation, and capital expenditures are not operating expenses.",
