        content: "**Step 1: the monthly payment.** The standard amortization formula is payment = loan \u00d7 monthly rate \u00f7 (1 \u2212 (1 + monthly rate)^\u2212number of payments). With a $900,000 loan at 7.5% over 25 years (300 payments), the monthly rate is 0.625%:\n\n$900,000 \u00d7 0.00625 \u00f7 (1 \u2212 1.00625^\u2212300) = **$6,651 per month**, or $79,811 per year.\n\n**Step 2: cash out over five years.**\n\n| Item | Amount |\n|---|---|\n| Down payment | $300,000 |\n| Purchase costs | $36,000 |\n| Mortgage payments (60 \u00d7 $6,651) | $399,055 |\n| Operating costs (5 \u00d7 $18,000) | $90,000 |\n| **Total cash out** | **$825,055** |\n\n**Step 3: what you own after five years.** After 60 payments the loan balance is $825,593. You have repaid $74,407 of principal and paid $324,648 of interest. The interest is the part that is gone; the principal is the part you keep.\n\n**Step 4: the sale.** The property is still worth $1,200,000 (flat prices). Selling costs are 6%, or $72,000. After paying off the $825,593 loan, the cash back in your hand is:\n\n$1,200,000 \u2212 $72,000 \u2212 $825,593 = **$302,407**\n\n**Step 5: net cost of buying for five years.**\n\n$825,055 cash out \u2212 $302,407 back = **$522,648**",
